  "result": "All 8 tests pass, including the 5 pre-existing ones.\n\n**What I changed** in `kvstore/store.py` (the SQLite-backed store from the prior session):\n\n- **Schema** now has an `ns` column, and the primary key is the pair `(ns, key)`, so the same key can hold different values in different namespaces. Still one table in one file, and no side files.\n- **`set`, `get`, `delete`, `keys`** each take `ns: str = \"default\"` and filter or upsert on both namespace and key. The upsert conflict target is the composite key.\n- **New `count(ns=\"default\")`** runs a `COUNT(*)` for that namespace.\n- **New `namespaces()`** returns `SELECT DISTINCT ns ... ORDER BY ns`, so a namespace disappears from the list as soon as its last key is deleted.\n- **Legacy migration** in `__init__`: if a data file still has the old single-column table, it is rebuilt into the new shape with every existing row placed in the default namespace. I verified this with an ad-hoc script: old rows survive, new namespaces work, reopening persists, and the directory still contains only the one data file.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was touched. `store.py` was already untracked before I started, so nothing is committed.",
